  timeout. Covered shapes:
    - 56 skip-record shapes: U+2003/U+3000/NBSP/NEL/U+1680/BOM in DETAIL, REASON, TASK
      and ATTEMPT; raw \xff/\x85/\xa0; VT/FF/CR; CRLF; NUL at 5 positions; first-match
      duplicates; indented and lower-case keys; empty files.
    - Non-regular skip entries: dir, FIFO, mode-000, dangling, loop, link-to-valid,
      link-to-FIFO, link-to-dir.
    - 17 Codex verdict-entry shapes: PASS, FAIL, PASS without MANIFEST_SHA256, no ---,
      bad FAMILY, bad TASK, dangling, loop, dir, FIFO, mode-000, links to PASS/FAIL/FIFO/dir,
      evidence only at an older attempt.
    - Other checkers' non-regular entries, judge panels, and two-consecutive-fails.
  Before trusting the harness I checked that it catches known-bad trees. On M-e it
  reported LOCALE SPLITs; on M-d(dash) and on a gate without `-L` it reported mismatches.
    GRID=1 run: rows=936, gate-accepted=396, mismatches=0, locale-splits=0,
      hangs/throws=0. The grid is tiers 1-3 x {tests,second,codex | tests,second}
      x every skip shape, plus every verdict-entry shape x 6 skip shapes.
    Random run, seed 2026: rows=1200, gate-accepted=363, locale-splits=0,
      hangs/throws=0, mismatches=2 plus 7 more of a second class. Both classes are
      pre-existing (F-1 and F-2).
  Probe 2 (rule 7, stats): an independent fixture with hand-computed expectations:
    - pairs at attempts 0..3, including an attempt-0 Codex FAIL;
    - a skip-only pair;
    - an invalid checker-second (FAMILY anthropicx);
    - a BOM skip, which reads as invalid;
    - a dotted sibling p4.1;
    - a verdict and a skip record at one attempt;
    - a no-change row;
    - a Codex verdict beyond the ledger attempt.
    Expected and got "codex: ran 5/6, FAIL 3, same-verdict-as-second 2, codex-only FAIL 2".
    All six per-task lines matched, e.g. "p2 ... codex=FAIL second=none".
    The output is byte-identical (cmp) under C, C.UTF-8 and en_US.UTF-8.
  Probe 3 (rule 9): for 240 grid rows I wrote each row as a single-row ledger and ran
